        "faq_power": {"type":"faq","settings":{"question":"The mirror does not power on. What should I check?","answer":"<p>Confirm the ignition is in ACC or ON, the 12-V battery terminal is connected, and both sides of the vehicle-specific T-harness are fully locked. Inspect the applicable vehicle fuse only after checking the connectors. Do not bypass a fuse or probe airbag wiring.</p>"}},
        "faq_rear_image": {"type":"faq","settings":{"question":"The display powers on, but there is no rear camera image.","answer":"<p>Power the vehicle off. Reseat the matching video connectors at the mirror and rear camera, then inspect the extension cable for a pinched section. Confirm the connector was not damaged while being pulled through the liftgate boot.</p>"}},
        "faq_brake": {"type":"faq","settings":{"question":"The camera works, but the third brake light does not illuminate.","answer":"<p>Do not drive until the brake light operates correctly. Recheck the original brake-light plug, its locking tab, and the retained factory fuse. If the connector or vehicle wiring differs from the guide, use a qualified automotive installer.</p>"}},
        "faq_mirror": {"type":"faq","settings":{"question":"Can the ClearDrive unit still be used as a conventional mirror?","answer":"<p>Yes. With the display off, the reflective surface can be used as a conventional mirror. Use the display or mode control supplied with your product version to switch views. Always adjust the mirror before driving.</p>"}}
      },
